area: model
case: 06-model-extremes
verification: explicit-divergence
oracle: python
projection: model
reason: pydantic holds a Python int of any width and FetchRequest.offset has no upper bound, so a 2**70 offset is accepted and re-encoded exactly; the port's decoder accepts a Yojson Int (or an integral Float) only and reports Intlit as a type error, so the same body is refused. Refusing is honest at a 63-bit int, but the sentence ('expected an integer, got an integer') is not — pinned and raised for the port's model layer.
